2.5  The binaries the installer distributes
-------------------------------------------

A LabCairn install brings in more than the npm packages §2.4 lists. The NSIS
installer embeds eight binaries of its own: seven NSIS plug-ins carried in the
installer's `$PLUGINSDIR`, and `elevate.exe`, which sits in the payload's
`resources/` directory.

Measured 2026-11-11 on the unsigned build of that date — `LabCairn Setup
0.0.0.exe`, 124,536,512 bytes, sha256
`da483fd949efba5e603bd8b47d0f57dfedd26f61b6469c69a59dac3e6e1241ea` — by
listing the archive with 7-Zip, extracting its members and hashing each one.
Every binary was then matched by sha256 against the two electron-builder
download caches the build fetches, and those two bundles are what say what
each binary's terms are.

`System.dll`, `nsDialogs.dll`, `nsExec.dll` and `elevate.exe` are
