5.3  Reproducing the shell figures
----------------------------------

The lead command this section used to name does not reproduce anything. Measured
2026-11-11 on copies of shell/package.json and shell/pnpm-lock.yaml outside the
repository, with node v24.16.0 and pnpm 9.15.9: `pnpm --dir shell list
--depth Infinity` with no installed tree prints 0 bytes on stdout, 0 bytes on
stderr, and exits 0. A reproduction section whose first command silently prints
an empty list is not a reproduction. The figures come out of the lockfile itself:

  # 1. the surface, read out of the lock — no install, no network, fresh checkout
  node .github/shell-lockfile-keys.mjs shell/pnpm-lock.yaml
    # packages_keys: 268   snapshots_keys: 268   union_keys: 273
    # peer_suffixed_keys: 5   distinct_name_version: 268   distinct_names: 241
    # names_at_more_than_one_version: 17
    # runtime_closure: 13   build_closure: 263   shared_by_both_closures: 8
    # build_only: 255   entries_in_neither_closure: 0   unresolved_edges: 0

  # 2. the same figures with the package manager, once installed
  pnpm --dir shell install --frozen-lockfile   # the tree this section is about
  pnpm --dir shell list --depth Infinity       # the resolved set

  # 3. each package's licence, from the registry and from its own tarball
  curl -fsS https://registry.npmjs.org/<name>/<version>   # licence identifier
  curl -fsS -o <pkg>.tgz <dist.tarball>                   # published tarball
  tar -tzf <pkg>.tgz                                       # its members
  tar -xzf <pkg>.tgz package/LICENSE                       # its licence file

**The name rule the licence-document counts depend on**, stated because a first
attempt got it wrong in both directions. A licence document is a member whose
**basename**, case-insensitively, is `LICENSE` / `LICENCE` / `UNLICENSE` /
`COPYING` / `NOTICE` / `COPYRIGHT`, optionally followed by a licence flavour
(`LICENSE-MIT.txt`, `LICENSE.WTFPL.txt`, `LICENSE.APACHE`, `LICENSE.BSD`), and
never a source-file extension. A rule that merely *contains* "license" counts
`app-builder-lib`'s `out/util/license.js` and `nsisLicense.js` — code that
generates an installer's licence *screen* — and misses the real documents whose
basename carries a suffix. Measured under the corrected rule: 252 of the 268
publish a document, 259 documents, 4 packages with more than one, 16 with none.

`shell/test/notice-licences.test.mjs` re-measures the 273 keys and the closure
split against §2.4 in both directions on every run, through this same reader: a
package adopted without a NOTICE row, a NOTICE row for a package that left the
lock, a drifted count and a copyleft class written into §2.4.3 all redden it.
Nothing on the npm side read licences at all before that file — §5.2's audit
resolves the Python closure with `uv export` and never opens `shell/`, and the
`shell.yml` job runs `node --test` with no pnpm step.

The per-package evidence — the registry record, the tarball integrity
comparison, the licence document text and the holder lines for all 268 — is in
the measurement record dated 2026-11-11 under
`E:/labcairn-local/phase3-g1-evidence/`, outside the repository, together with
the scripts that produced it.


5.4  Reproducing the installer-binary and web-tree figures
------------------------------------------------------------

The eight installer binaries live in the build product, not in the repository,
so their commands start from a build. The web tree's lock figures need
neither a build nor an install; its licence classes do.

**The eight installer binaries.**

  # 1. the build. `shell/electron-builder.yml` copies `web/dist` into the
  #    package as `resources/web-dist` and writes its output to the directory
  #    LABCAIRN_SHELL_DIST_DIR names — a directory outside the repository. The
  #    build refuses when `web/dist` is absent (`beforeBuild:` names the guard),
  #    so the web bundle is built first.
  pnpm --dir shell install --frozen-lockfile
  pnpm --dir web install --frozen-lockfile
  pnpm --dir web run build
  LABCAIRN_SHELL_DIST_DIR=<dir> pnpm --dir shell run dist   # electron-builder --win
